 "_redact_dataclass_viewer": "A data change, no code change (2026-10-27): the dataclass-viewer case now holds SYNTHETIC values (DEMO_FACILITY). Its two entries are rewritten from 9bb1818's build (the build before the speed work) with the new case files copied in; 283145c's build writes the same two, and the other 51 views unchanged.",
 "_merge_toolbar_mix": "A deliberate output change (merge of lane/toolbar-mix @ 18c5638 onto main 1e73a7a, 2026-10-27): toolbar-mix changes the table's drawn HTML (selection, CONTRACT §15) and branched before this oracle existed. Rewritten from 18c5638's own build (before the table speed work 6265d06) over the merged gallery, now all 106 table and pivot views (was 53); the merged build draws all 106 byte for byte the same.",
 "_p0_blockers": "lane/p0-blockers (PEP 0010 P0, 2026-10-28): a deliberate output change of the table, two parts. (1) The spacer below the drawn rows counts the scroll margin once (getTotalSize() - (end - margin)), so it is taller by the margin (the header, 30 px here) in every table with rows below the window, and the mid capture's scroll position moves with the longer box. (2) A table with no column to draw (a dashboard view opened over the file's top-level data) draws one cell naming the columns its data lacks instead of 0 px rows. 79 entries changed, 31 unchanged. Written from integrate/packet 8eb8480's build (the code before) with the change applied by its spec, never from the code under test: the spacer is the sum of the planned sizes of the rows after the last one drawn (the virtualiser's own plan, read in the old page), the empty state is the spec's sentence; the old build was captured at the scroll position the new build's mid capture reached (the two map a scrollTop to the same rows). The code under test then matched all 122 views byte for byte (top and mid).",
 "_public_export_paths": "A gallery data change, no code change (lane/home-paths, 2026-10-30): robotparts-sources' sources.json shows ~/ instead of ~/ in its 'How it refreshes' column (the redaction tools/publish-site.mjs and tools/public-export.mjs apply), so the public snapshot draws the same as this tree. Two entries moved: robotparts-sources :: By kind and :: Needs refresh (top and mid; status and row count unchanged, bytes 41986 -> 41730 and 14530 -> 14466); the other 108 entries are unchanged. Written by table_oracle_checks.py --write from main d662f09's build (the code before) over the new gallery, never from the code under test. Measured: d662f09's build over d662f09's gallery equals this golden on every entry; d662f09's build and the lane's build (which changes nothing under packages/) write identical digests over the new gallery on all 170 views.",
 "_dashboard_cards": "lane/dashboard-cards (CONTRACT §25): the round-2 rebuilds changed three existing tables' .base (pid-tuning 'Every joint', vibetracks-runs 'Runs' and 'By track': declared rounding and plain-text labels) and added 4 tables. Those entries are written by table_oracle_checks.py --write from main 5472d02's build (the code before) over the new gallery, never from the code under test; every other entry is unchanged.",
 "_table_digits": "lane/table-digits (CONTRACT §17 declared rounding, 2026-10-29): a table cell, its summary row, its stats parts and its range now write a property's declared digits/compact like the KPI cards and list/cards/board cells already did. Two entries moved, both vibetracks-runs (its pass_rate declares digits: 3): Runs and By track (every pass_rate cell and the By track Average summary: 0.7091 -> 0.709, 0.9898 -> 0.99, 0.6182 -> 0.618). Derived from integrate/packet 6adff6c's build (the code before) with the change applied by spec, never from the code under test: that build's captured HTML had every pass_rate cell and summary number rewritten to 3 significant figures (integer part never cut, trailing zeros dropped, thousands separators) by an independent Decimal implementation, then digested; the fixed build draws those two byte for byte the same (top e2e4b55f7a38b1c7 / mid b9b1d82fc3a670a6; top 67b4812c3e02f332). The other 109 entries are unchanged.",
 "_types": "EXCEPTION to the rule above, recorded and reviewed (lane/types, CONTRACT §28; Zach, 2026-10-28: \"This looks great merge it\"): written from the merged build, because the drawing is the deliberate change (the table's lines, header cells, typed cells, a header tab stop) and the commit before cannot draw types. Every view drawn is pinned (the check asserts the golden's keys equal the views drawn; main's golden pinned 110 of them). Before accepting it, docs/review_table_oracle.py drew every table and pivot view with main 54580f2's build and this one, and compared rows by identity and order, columns, header labels, units, group labels, untyped cell text and typed cell text against an independent formatter: 175 views, 162 declared changes only, 3 new (property-types), 10 flagged, every one the same in both builds: 9 draw no <table> row in either (dashboard panels the review's table probe cannot read), and map-annotations has two views named Figures, so the review mounts its map in both. Per-view results: reports/media/types/oracle-review.json in the main checkout.",
